# The BBS proof of bbs-proof.rel, with a sound statement and an
# environment that breaks it.
#
# This is the more faithful reading of what the draft forbids.  Its
# generators are derived by create_generators, so a designer writes
# H_j1 and H_j2 as distinct names and the derivation supplies the
# elements.  "The generators MUST be unique" is therefore a
# requirement on the derivation -- on the environment -- and not on
# the statement, which is written correctly either way.
#
# So the statement below is the sound one, and the instance collapses
# the two message generators onto a single element.  The statement
# check passes and the instance check does not, which is exactly the
# division Compiler/DslInstantiate.v draws.
#
# bbs-proof-colliding-generators.rel models the other failure: a
# designer who writes one generator twice.  Both are worth having,
# because the draft's sentence covers only this one.
secrets e r1 r3 m_j1 m_j2
claims  e r1 r3 m_j1 m_j2
eq  Bbar   Abar  D   1  1     1
eq  Bv     1     1   D  H_j1  H_j2

point Abar  2
point D     3
point H_j1  5
point H_j2  5
